		bodyHtml: `<p>The petition cannot be separated from the address that comes immediately before it. In the Father&rsquo;s Heart Bible, Matthew 6:9 reads: &ldquo;This, then, is how you should pray: &lsquo;Our Father in heaven, hallowed be your name.&rsquo;&rdquo; Luke&rsquo;s shorter version is starker still: &ldquo;When you pray, say: Father, hallowed be your name.&rdquo;</p><p>The name being hallowed is the name <em>Father</em>. That is the striking thing about the prayer and it is easy to read past. Jesus does not teach His followers to open with a title of power. He gives them the word He Himself used, and then asks that <em>that</em> name &mdash; Father &mdash; be honoured as holy.</p><p>Holiness and intimacy are not in competition in this sentence. The One who is nearest is also the One who is holy, and the prayer holds both in a single breath.</p>`,
