		bodyHtml: `<p>Because &ldquo;hallowed be your name&rdquo; is a request, it can be prayed rather than only recited. Three things it asks for, in the order the prayer itself suggests:</p><ul><li><strong>That He be known as He actually is</strong> &mdash; not as a distant power or a rule-giver, but as the Father the rest of Scripture reveals.</li><li><strong>That His name be honoured in us</strong> &mdash; that the people who call Him Father do not make that name mean something false to those watching.</li><li><strong>That His name be honoured everywhere</strong> &mdash; which is why the very next line is &ldquo;your kingdom come.&rdquo; The two petitions are one movement.</li></ul><p>Read in full, the prayer moves from who He is, to what He is doing, to what we need &mdash; and it begins by settling the first question before asking anything.</p>`,
